BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (Rotary and Learned Positional Encodings for Long-Context Transformers: A) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Study) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Priya Nair, Tomasz Wojcik, and Hana Lindqvist) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Synthetic Sequence Modelling Group. All content is fictional and produced) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (solely as a retrieval evaluation fixture.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Abstract) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Positional encodings determine how far a Transformer can extrapolate beyond) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (its training context. This synthetic study compares learned absolute) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (embeddings, sinusoidal encodings, and rotary variants on a controlled next-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (token prediction task with procedurally generated sequences. We introduce the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Helix-64 rotary schedule and show that it extends stable extrapolation to) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (131072 tokens while keeping perplexity drift below 2.1% at the extrapolation) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (frontier.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (1 Introduction) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Transformers are permutation-invariant unless positional information is) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (injected. The choice of positional encoding therefore controls both in-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (distribution behaviour and length generalization, and it has become one of the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (most consequential design decisions in long-context modelling.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (This study is organized as follows. Section 2 reviews positional encoding) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (families. Section 3 defines the Helix-64 schedule. Section 4 describes the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (experimental protocol, Section 5 reports results, and Sections 6 and 7 discuss) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (limitations and conclusions.) Tj T* ET
