BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (2 Families of Positional Encodings) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Learned absolute embeddings assign a trainable vector to each position; they) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (are simple and effective within the training window but cannot represent) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (positions never seen during training. Sinusoidal encodings replace learned) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (vectors with fixed trigonometric functions, offering unbounded range with weak) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (extrapolation. Rotary encodings apply position-dependent rotations to query) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (and key vectors, making attention scores depend on relative offsets.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (A recurring limitation of standard rotary encodings is that high-frequency) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (components wrap around quickly, so attention logits become noisy once) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (sequences exceed the training length. Frequency scaling and interpolation) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (mitigate this but distort short-range behaviour.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (3 The Helix-64 Schedule) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (The Helix-64 rotary schedule assigns rotation frequencies geometrically across) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (64 bands and anneals the highest band during training so that no band) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (completes a full revolution within the training window. In our synthetic) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (protocol, Helix-64 extends stable extrapolation to 131072 tokens, four times) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (the training length of 32768 tokens, while keeping perplexity drift below 2.1%) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (at the extrapolation frontier.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (The schedule adds no parameters and no inference-time cost relative to) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (standard rotary encodings. Its only hyperparameter is the annealing horizon,) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (which we fix at the final ten percent of training steps throughout this study.) Tj T* ET
