BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (6 Limitations) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Our sequences are generated by a Markov grammar, so the results measure length) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (generalization under controlled dependencies rather than natural language. The) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (annealing horizon was not tuned per encoding, which may understate competing) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (methods. We also do not study interaction with attention sinks or sliding-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (window attention.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (7 Conclusions) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Positional encoding choice dominates long-context extrapolation. The Helix-64) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (rotary schedule extends stable extrapolation to 131072 tokens with perplexity) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (drift below 2.1% in our synthetic setting, at no additional cost. Future work) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (should test the schedule on natural corpora and combine it with memory-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (augmented attention.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf () Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (References) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([1] P. Nair and H. Lindqvist. Frequency annealing in rotary encodings. Journal) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (of Synthetic Sequence Modelling, 2026. Fictional reference.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([2] T. Wojcik. Controlled benchmarks for length generalization. Synthetic) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Workshop on Long Contexts, 2025. Fictional reference.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf ([3] E. Duarte. A taxonomy of positional information. Transactions on Synthetic) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Learning, 2024. Fictional reference.) Tj T* ET
